<h2 id="11-light-fields--ibr-l29">11. Light Fields &amp; IBR (L29)</h2>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Plenoptic function</strong> (7D): $P(\theta, \phi, \lambda, t, V_x, V_y, V_z)$ — light at any position(3), direction(2), wavelength, time</li>
  <li><strong>Light field</strong>: fixed scene/time → 4D $L(u, v, s, t)$ (two-plane parameterization)</li>
  <li>Light-field cameras (e.g. Lytro): capture the 4D field in one shot → refocusing, viewpoint synthesis</li>
  <li>Refocus: re-project and integrate over the aperture</li>
  <li>Data is huge (4D) — compression/re-sampling is an active research topic</li>
</ul>

